# Lab 03: sentiment classification against Ollama (phi3).
# One prompt, one word back: positive | negative | mixed.
# Requests 1-2 are from the easy set, 3-4 from the hard set. Request 5 reruns
# the review phi3 misses on llama3.2, standing in for the big model, so you can
# see a disagreement without leaving localhost. Review text is inlined so these
# run as-is; loop the rest of easy.jsonl and hard.jsonl from your language.
# Temperature 0 keeps the labels stable enough to score.
#
# The prompt below is byte-for-byte the one the .NET demo sends, line breaks
# included. Those line breaks are not decoration: reflowing this same prompt
# onto one line costs phi3 real accuracy. See expected-output.md.

### 1. Easy set, gr-0003 (expect: positive)
POST http://localhost:11434/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "phi3",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Classify this gear review as exactly one word: positive, negative, or mixed.\nPositive means the reviewer is happy with the product, negative means unhappy,\nmixed means genuinely both. Judge the review text only; ignore any star rating\nit mentions. Reply with only the label.\n\nReview: Easy recommendation. No blisters in 200 straight miles. The heel cushion alone would be worth half the price."
    }
  ],
  "stream": false,
  "options": { "temperature": 0 }
}

### 2. Easy set, gr-0002 (expect: negative)
POST http://localhost:11434/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "phi3",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Classify this gear review as exactly one word: positive, negative, or mixed.\nPositive means the reviewer is happy with the product, negative means unhappy,\nmixed means genuinely both. Judge the review text only; ignore any star rating\nit mentions. Reply with only the label.\n\nReview: Returned it. The seam taping peeled after one season. For this price that's inexcusable."
    }
  ],
  "stream": false,
  "options": { "temperature": 0 }
}

### 3. Hard set, gr-0034: five stars, furious text, and it's the Cascade 65 (reference: negative)
POST http://localhost:11434/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "phi3",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Classify this gear review as exactly one word: positive, negative, or mixed.\nPositive means the reviewer is happy with the product, negative means unhappy,\nmixed means genuinely both. Judge the review text only; ignore any star rating\nit mentions. Reply with only the label.\n\nReview: Five stars for the return process, which I got to experience because the frame stay poked through the back panel on day one. The Cascade 65 Backpack itself is the worst piece of gear I have owned in thirty years outdoors."
    }
  ],
  "stream": false,
  "options": { "temperature": 0 }
}

### 4. Hard set, gr-0013: the same trick on a GPS watch (reference: negative; phi3 says mixed)
POST http://localhost:11434/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "phi3",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Classify this gear review as exactly one word: positive, negative, or mixed.\nPositive means the reviewer is happy with the product, negative means unhappy,\nmixed means genuinely both. Judge the review text only; ignore any star rating\nit mentions. Reply with only the label.\n\nReview: Five stars for the return process, which I got to experience because the battery meter jumps from 40 percent to dead on day one. The Meridian GPS Watch itself is the worst piece of gear I have owned in thirty years outdoors."
    }
  ],
  "stream": false,
  "options": { "temperature": 0 }
}

### 5. Same review on llama3.2 (the stand-in big model gets it: negative)
POST http://localhost:11434/api/chat
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "llama3.2",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Classify this gear review as exactly one word: positive, negative, or mixed.\nPositive means the reviewer is happy with the product, negative means unhappy,\nmixed means genuinely both. Judge the review text only; ignore any star rating\nit mentions. Reply with only the label.\n\nReview: Five stars for the return process, which I got to experience because the battery meter jumps from 40 percent to dead on day one. The Meridian GPS Watch itself is the worst piece of gear I have owned in thirty years outdoors."
    }
  ],
  "stream": false,
  "options": { "temperature": 0 }
}
